so just as dc was finally starting to  produce some really really good content  with shows like peacemaker and movies  like the batman and upcoming exciting  projects like black adam  warner brothers goes and merges with  discovery now being called warner bros  discovery and apparently some big  changes are coming to dc it sounds like  dc is actually looking for their own  kevin feige type of figure to run things  over at dc now marvel studios has  obviously been crushing it kevin feige  is definitely the one to get credit  there's a lot of people involved but we  know that kevin feige's at the helm does  it make sense for dc to have somebody  like this or could this be a bad idea  depending on your views this could be a  really good thing for dc or it could be  a really bad thing for to see now  variety released an article that has  exclusive details about what dc is  thinking and apparently  it could get a complete  overhaul  what's going on everybody it's warren  welcome back to the cosmic wonder we  normally talk marvel but i love dc too  and this is some pretty big news so  let's go over this article and talk  about what exactly this means now it  starts off by saying the new owners of  all things batman superman and wonder  woman are exploring an overhaul of dc  entertainment it says before the merger  closed zazlav who is the ceo now vetted  candidates with experience in creating  and nurturing blockbuster intellectual  property with the goal of potentially  finding someone to serve as a creative  and strategic czar similar to what  marvel has in kevin feige now right away  people have kind of been making this  comparison for a pretty long time now  people have been saying dc needs  somebody like kevin feige that is in  charge of everything somebody who has a  vision but right off the bat here's the  thing about kevin feige  he's a huge comic book fan  he really is into everything that he  does and i think the problem with dc has  been is that it's really been run by a  company it's been ran by a lot of  different people throwing a lot of  different suggestions out there and i  think the success that they found  recently was letting people kind of do  their own thing having these directors  come in and these writers come in like  james gunn go this is what i got from  the comics i'm a screenwriter i'm a  developer i produce things i know what  to do just let me do it they let them do  it and then magic happens like the  peacemaker show which was fantastic the  article continues to say insiders say  that zaslav believes that the success of  the merger one that has left the company  highly leveraged will rest in no small  part on unlocking the potential of dc  comics universe of characters discovery  insiders believe that although dc has  achieved cinematic success with recent  films such as aquaman and the batman it  lacks a coherent creative and brand  strategy discovery believes that several  top shelf characters such as superman  have been left to languish and need to  be revitalized they also believe that  projects like todd phillips's joker are  a shining example of how second build  characters from dc library can and  should be exploited margot robbie's  harley quinn is another example now  he's not wrong here what he says is it  lacks coherent creative and brand  strategy and i think this was kind of  the problem the strategy kind of seemed  like it was all over the place now  what's really sad is it seems like some  future projects might actually be  affected by this when the flash it was  kind of supposed to explain everything  that dc had under their belts it was  supposed to show us what the plan was  how everything kind of operated now  not everything needs to be a marvel  cinematic universe i think one off  things like the batman and the joker or  joker  i think one-off things like the batman  and joker they work and they kind of  work because they are one-off yes you  can create other universes within these  projects like gotham city police show  that's coming out you can create other  things within that universe but not  everything has to be connected i think  these films worked because they weren't  but then you have things like the  suicide squad and the spin-off the  peacemaker series that they also work as  well i don't think they need to be  copying marvel but i do think they do  need to hone in on a better plan but dc  isn't exactly the best at making good  judgment calls for comic book characters  and i think that's because the people  who are behind all decisions aren't  exactly true comic book fans like i said  kevin feige he's deep in the comments he  kevin feige he's deep in the comics he's  read all of these comics he knows what  he's talking about he knows how to make  everything work so i do kind of agree  with what they're talking about here  they should have somebody come in but  unless that person is pretty much  exactly like kevin feige but with dc  comics i don't think that it's going to  work i think the only other option is  you bring in people for projects that  are like that like i mentioned before  james gunn zack snyder these worked the  fandom really does enjoy the films that  these people make i think if they wanted  to go that route it might actually be  better for them now it seems like they  have always lacked a brand strategy now  when they first came out with the  justice league it almost seemed like  they were trying to be different than  marvel like very very obviously  blatantly different than marvel marvel  started off by introducing these  characters they put them all in a  universe where they exist and then they  brought them together they came in to  the avengers not knowing each other kind  of have an idea of who they are because  they existed in the same universe and  then they worked together then they kept  doing their own thing then they brought  them back together dc went and did the  opposite they brought everybody together  with without really introducing anybody  and then they went let's now do like  their own things it's something that  could have worked if they had a better  idea of what they really wanted to do  and unfortunately i think they just  really didn't know at the time now the  biggest thing here is that i think they  want a connected universe but i don't  think they have to do that like i  mentioned i think they should go kind of  twofold here i think they should  continue to make their one-off projects  because i think those projects are  really really good i really like the  one-off projects and i think if they  continue to do that they will have a lot  of success and they will make good films  however i do like the idea of having a  connected universe it doesn't have to be  on as big of a scale that marvel does it  but it can be connected because let's  face it we all love to see batman  interact with superman with wonder woman  we love to see all of that  now the article goes on to say that one  insider suggested that zaslov was less  interested in finding a creative guru  and more eager to hire someone who had  the type of business background needed  to keep all the different factions of dc  working more harmoniously  that could work again i don't think they  have to choose between either or i think  they could do both but this could  definitely work because they definitely  seem to lack harmony between all of  their properties most of the time people  don't even know what dc is doing  they put so many projects out there and  some are connected and some are but also  are in some weird way at the same time  they have multiple different jokers  going on right now there's multiple  different versions of some characters  it's just kind of a mess right now and  again the flash was supposed to kind of  explain everything and i think the flash  can do a very good job at setting up dc  for a very successful future because  they are introducing a multiverse and  that opens up a lot of different  possibilities and it also makes it to  where everything can be connected  without having to really be connected  that's the cool thing about the  multiverse kind of anything is possible  but the big question is right now who  exactly do they need to come in what can  they actually get from somebody  overlooking everything one i do think  they need this person but only if it's  the right person and two i do think this  person needs to realize that everything  can exist in a large multiverse but  still be one off i think that is going  to be a key to the success of dc because  they can't copy marvel studios  everyone's just going to compare it and  don't get me wrong i love dc characters  batman is actually my favorite superhero  as much as i talk about marvel batman is  my favorite but what do you think dc  actually needs at this point in time do  you think they need a kevin feige type  person or do you think they need to  bring in people like james gunn and zack  snyder and just kind of let them do  their thing let me know what you think  about this in the comments down below  are you a fan of dc and if you are do  you like how things are going so far or  do you think they actually need this  overhaul let me know what you think in  the comments down below don't forget to  like the video and subscribe so you  don't miss out on any of the latest news  as always thank you all so much for  watching woof  [Music]
 

